  "language": "en",
  "question": {
    "prompt": "The smallest of 3 consecutive integers is \\(n\\), so the integers, in order, are \\(n\\), \\(n+1\\), and \\(n+2\\). Their sum can be expressed using a letter. When \\(n=7\\), what is the sum of these 3 integers?"
  },
  "schemaVersion": "3.0",
  "solutions": [
    {
      "directNodeIds": [
        "cnm_027",
        "cnm_034",
        "cnm_029"
      ],
      "explanation": "Their sum is \\(n+(n+1)+(n+2)=3n+3\\). When \\(n=7\\), it is \\(3\\times7+3=24\\) (that is, \\(7+8+9=24\\)).",
      "id": "m1",
